Subject: Isolate live kubeconfig and require namespace for live snapshots

Why: In `live` mode, upstream's `get-credentials` setup mutates the default host kubeconfig (`agents/platform/AGENTS.md` requires a per-target `KUBECONFIG` under `$HERMES_HOME/.kubeconfigs/`), and omitting `--namespace` causes `snapshot.py` to issue `kubectl get ...,jobs,pods,events -A -o json`, which `kubectl-admit` refuses on `fleet`-tier installs. Requiring per-target `KUBECONFIG` isolation and `--namespace <ns>` keeps `live` mode safe in kube-agents.
Local-Issue: none (adoption of gke-kueue-troubleshooting from google/skills)
Eval-Case: kueue-troubleshooting-mixed-flavor-tas-probe
Upstream-Issue: none (specific to this repository)
Retire-When: never; per-target kubeconfig layout and sandbox kubectl admission are this repository's

diff --git a/SKILL.md b/SKILL.md
--- a/SKILL.md
+++ b/SKILL.md
@@ -32,11 +32,10 @@ MUST read and follow the instructions in
   `/opt/data/profiles/platform/skills/gke-kueue-troubleshooting/scripts/` and
   require no cloud SDKs; always invoke them by full path with `python3` because
   kanban workers start in their card workspace, not the skill directory). In
-  `live` mode, follow "Before you begin" in
-  [Deploy a batch system using Kueue](https://docs.cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/tutorials/kueue-intro.md.txt)
-  to initialize `gcloud` and select the target project, and follow
-  [Install kubectl and configure cluster access](https://docs.cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/how-to/cluster-access-for-kubectl.md.txt)
-  to configure cluster credentials (`offline_data` and `logs_archive` read local
+  `live` mode, never mutate the default host kubeconfig: export a per-target
+  `KUBECONFIG="${HERMES_HOME:-/opt/data}/.kubeconfigs/kubeconfig_${PROJECT}_${CLUSTER}_${LOCATION}.yaml"`
+  before running `gcloud container clusters get-credentials` for any non-host
+  cluster (see `gke-basics`; `offline_data` and `logs_archive` read local
   files only).
 - **Cloud Billing and APIs**: For `live` cluster inspection or Cloud Logging
   exports, ensure the project has an active Cloud Billing account and the Google
@@ -125,7 +124,10 @@ bundle files (at most **twice**). Never read the skill's own Python scripts.
    - `live` / `offline_data`: run
      `python3 /opt/data/profiles/platform/skills/gke-kueue-troubleshooting/scripts/snapshot.py`
      with `--mode <mode> --action snapshot --ledger-path <ledger>` (add
-     `--namespace <ns>` if known; `--kueue-namespace` if not `kueue-system`;
+     `--namespace <ns>` — required in `live` mode; if unknown, discover it first
+     with `kubectl get workloads.kueue.x-k8s.io -A` so `snapshot.py` does not
+     run a cluster-wide `pods`/`events` JSON dump that sandbox `kubectl`
+     admission refuses on large fleets; `--kueue-namespace` if not `kueue-system`;
      `--ignore-namespaces ns1,ns2` for extra add-on namespaces). If no active
      `Workload`/`Job` is present or controller/audit history is needed, also run
      `python3 /opt/data/profiles/platform/skills/gke-kueue-troubleshooting/scripts/trace_logs.py --mode <mode> --ledger-path <ledger>`
